# Infrastructure & CI

- Keep services independently deployable. Reuse Compose profiles (`full`, `observability`, `web`) and existing healthchecks/depends_on.
- Never put real secrets in Compose, CI logs, or committed env files—placeholders in `.env.example` only.
- Dockerfiles stay multi-stage/production-oriented. Do not delete volumes/user data for routine verification.
- Observability (Prometheus scrape, OTel→Tempo, Grafana datasources) must match actual app instrumentation (`management.otlp`, Micrometer).
- GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): preserve compose-config, frontend lint/build, and per-service Maven tests. Do not weaken gates for speed without explicit approval.
- Prefer scoped script changes under `scripts/`; document new env vars as placeholders only.
